## Remaining qualifications

### 1. The graph route may be closer to an abstract `C1` proof than ER017 states

For an abstract existence theorem, finite atlas constants need not be numerically evaluated; finiteness plus strict inequalities and suitable shrinkings can suffice. Lemmas T.1–T.7 substantially repair the logical structure. Nevertheless, the user-designated final audit expressly leaves G4’s complete chart estimates and the exact regularity/uniqueness framework unfinished. The program therefore retains the external-theorem template rather than promoting the construction.

### 2. `C1` continuity at time zero needs exact restricted-cocycle justification

T.5’s argument is plausible because the unit tangent bundle of the compact finite-dimensional graph is compact and RFDE variational solution operators are strongly continuous. A final proof should cite or establish joint continuity of `(s,z,xi)->D Phi^s(z)xi` on that compact tangent bundle. It must not assert operator-norm convergence on an open subset of the full history space.

### 3. BLZ bibliography remains wrong

The audit cites “Existence and persistence of invariant manifolds for semiflows in Banach space” as TAMS 351 (1999), 4341–4368. The verified work with that title is Memoirs AMS 135 (1998), no. 645. Related sources are the 1999 CPAM overflowing-manifold paper and 2000 TAMS invariant-foliations paper. The controlling theorem must be selected and matched from the correct source.

### 4. Delay rescaling remains conditional on model structure

Time normalization to `[-1,0]` does not automatically make an arbitrary history functional smoothly parameter-dependent in delay on `C0`. For a discrete-delay model whose normalized functional is explicitly smooth, the route can work; otherwise use an exact varying-delay theorem or leave the parameter match open.

### 5. Spectral-stability wording

Complementary stability must concern every root of the full coupled characteristic operator after perturbation. Persistence should be justified by RFDE root localization/spectral perturbation, not “Rouché on a left half-plane contour.”

### 6. Equilibrium Jacobian convention

Under `Delta(lambda)=lambda I-L(e^{lambda·}I)`, the finite-dimensional equilibrium Jacobian is `-Delta(0)`. Invertibility is equivalent, but signs should remain consistent.

## Final accepted hierarchy

### Proved under stated assumptions

- finite-time mismatch-aware tracking;
- forward slack tube with confinement and valid RFDE mild-solution formulation;
- equilibrium branch from invertibility at zero;
- simple characteristic-crossing curve.

### Conditional external theorem

- compact `C1` Banach-semiflow NAIM/NHIM persistence under exact geometry, splitting, domination, perturbation, boundary, and localization hypotheses;
- vertical graph only after compact-embedding stability of the projected base;
- local nonlinear Hopf branch only after exact source matching and fixed-space parameterization;
- full orbital stability only with stable full complementary spectrum.

### Unverified/conjectural for concrete A021

- existence of a compact binding NAIM and numerical rates;
- concrete vertical invariant graph;
- concrete nonlinear Hopf coefficient and branch stability;
- any graph over a nonmanifold attractor or the full history cube.

## Implementation decision

No A021 manuscript implementation is authorized from ER017 alone. ER017 closes the announced audit batch and confirms the expanded conservative adjudication. A later source revision should implement only the jointly approved hierarchy, not any reviewer’s replacement text verbatim.